{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"id":"JFrog.Conan","latestVersion":"2.34.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"An open source, decentralized C/C++ package manager, to automate building and sharing of packages.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/conan-io/conan/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"An open source, decentralized C/C++ package manager, to automate building and sharing of packages.","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/conan-io/conan/blob/HEAD/LICENSE.md","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Conan is a package manager for C and C++ developers:\n- It is fully decentralized. Users can host their packages on their servers, privately. Integrates with Artifactory and Bintray.\n- Portable. Works across all platforms, including Linux, OSX, Windows (with native and first-class support, WSL, MinGW), Solaris, FreeBSD, embedded and cross-compiling, docker, WSL\n- Manage binaries. It can create, upload and download binaries for any configuration and platform, even cross-compiling, saving lots of time in development and continuous integration. The binary compatibility can be configured and customized. Manage all your artifacts in the same way on all platforms.\n- Integrates with any build system, including any proprietary and custom one. Provides tested support for major build systems (CMake, MSBuild, Makefiles, Meson, etc).\n- Extensible: Its Python-based recipes, together with extension points allow for great power and flexibility.\n- Large and active community, especially in GitHub (https://github.com/conan-io/conan) and Slack (https://cppalliance.org/slack/ #conan channel). This community also creates and maintains packages in ConanCenter and Bincrafters repositories in Bintray.\n- Stable. Used in production by many companies, since 1.0 there is a commitment not to break package recipes and documented behavior.","name":"Conan Package Manager","packageUrl":"https://conan.io/","publisher":"JFrog","publisherUrl":"https://conan.io/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/conan-io/conan/releases/tag/2.34.0","tags":["c","c++","cmake","conancenter","multi-platform","open-source","package-manager","packagemanager","python","software-repository","softwarerepository"]}},"longDescription":"Conan is a package manager for C and C++ developers:\n- It is fully decentralized. Users can host their packages on their servers, privately. Integrates with Artifactory and Bintray.\n- Portable. Works across all platforms, including Linux, OSX, Windows (with native and first-class support, WSL, MinGW), Solaris, FreeBSD, embedded and cross-compiling, docker, WSL\n- Manage binaries. It can create, upload and download binaries for any configuration and platform, even cross-compiling, saving lots of time in development and continuous integration. The binary compatibility can be configured and customized. Manage all your artifacts in the same way on all platforms.\n- Integrates with any build system, including any proprietary and custom one. Provides tested support for major build systems (CMake, MSBuild, Makefiles, Meson, etc).\n- Extensible: Its Python-based recipes, together with extension points allow for great power and flexibility.\n- Large and active community, especially in GitHub (https://github.com/conan-io/conan) and Slack (https://cppalliance.org/slack/ #conan channel). This community also creates and maintains packages in ConanCenter and Bincrafters repositories in Bintray.\n- Stable. Used in production by many companies, since 1.0 there is a commitment not to break package recipes and documented behavior.","name":"Conan Package Manager","packageUrl":"https://conan.io/","publisher":"JFrog","publisherUrl":"https://conan.io/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/conan-io/conan/releases/tag/2.34.0","tags":["c","c++","cmake","conancenter","multi-platform","open-source","package-manager","packagemanager","python","software-repository","softwarerepository"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.34.0/app.json","detailSha256":"81789ff38dfc2b53044972f39a6ad6b1c8de850556f5cf330cc24274cb66b3a4","releaseDate":"2026-10-28","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.34.0"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.33.0/app.json","detailSha256":"93b93b72f3866c537713bb1bf6fabf076d8b06904ae7fb543e5b01d06e1b4e5d","releaseDate":"2026-09-29","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.33.0"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.32.0/app.json","detailSha256":"a589e921f76749c7f0f272810765d9fed7137c033aff4b1d0b82b4aece01b686","releaseDate":"2026-08-31","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.32.0"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.31.2/app.json","detailSha256":"f24142ee4f3a66671c30bc410984856fb504f0e55a61ffb46874be8534a6010f","releaseDate":"2026-08-04","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.31.2"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.31.1/app.json","detailSha256":"0aa41a5c0e43472778bf39f78a0de05ae8b7d9b1c8e2e0d2ef29919c82fd155f","releaseDate":"2026-07-24","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.31.1"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.31.0/app.json","detailSha256":"8b88446b17962f46976eb089783050990fd6036c886edc5a5e7d88bd67017277","releaseDate":"2026-07-23","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.31.0"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.30.0/app.json","detailSha256":"848ce41792d58ce858570403d5a7efc11ee79737559388a60a475cee0c9d820a","releaseDate":"2026-06-29","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.30.0"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.29.1/app.json","detailSha256":"989008b8fdf7b45f48c77407289a2646c47284b7b2fd3c802f89080e2ce57a3f","releaseDate":"2026-06-12","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"2.29.1"},{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"detailPath":"versions/2.29.0/app.json","detailSha256":"3856f67580